SOMA-JAX is a derivative work: it reimplements SOMA-X (v0.3.3) — its body,
hand and SMPL-family layers, identity backends, skeletal and mesh-topology
abstractions, procedural rig, pose correctives, pose inversion, smoothing, I/O
and tools — in JAX/equinox in place of the upstream PyTorch + NVIDIA Warp
backend. Rig data, algorithms and API shape derive from SOMA-X. Upstream SOMA-X
is included unmodified at `third_party/SOMA-X` as a git submodule and retains
its own LICENSE. `tools/vis_pyrender.py` and `tools/make_teaser.py` are copied
from SOMA-X's `tools/`, keeping its copyright headers: the first with only a
docstring added, the second with only a docstring and an import path changed.

Summary of changes relative to SOMA-X, as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b):
see `docs/FAITHFULNESS.md`, which records what corresponds to what and how
closely it is measured to agree, what differs by design, which upstream defects
are not reproduced, what SOMA-JAX adds, and what is not ported.

